# Setup — {{project_name}}

Everything needed to reproduce the project is pinned in the repository:

| File | Pins |
|---|---|
| `environment.yml` | Python and every package the code imports (conda + pip) |
| `renv.lock`, `renv/activate.R`, `.Rprofile` | every R package the R code uses |
| `project.mk` (`CMDSTAN_VERSION`) | the CmdStan release used by cmdstanr and cmdstanpy |
| `.pre-commit-config.yaml` | the git hooks: gate, tests, notes, commit rules |
| `Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore` | all of the above in one image |

## Fresh machine

Requirements: git, make, conda (Miniforge or Miniconda; mamba is used when
present), R at the version recorded in `renv.lock`, and a C++ toolchain for
CmdStan.

```bash
make setup && make all
```

`make setup` runs, in order:

1. `make env` — creates the conda environment from `environment.yml`
   (updates it when it exists). Override the location with `ENV_PREFIX=/path`.
2. `make renv` — `renv::restore()` from `renv.lock` into `renv/library`.
3. `make cmdstan` — installs CmdStan `CMDSTAN_VERSION` into `~/.cmdstan`
   (skipped when already present; override with `CMDSTAN_DIR`).
4. `make hooks` — installs the pre-commit, pre-push and commit-msg hooks.

## Day to day

```bash
make check        # gate + Python and R tests + notes check
make all          # the full pipeline, then the site
make step M=pkg.module
make site && make serve
make help         # every target
```

The targets use the project environment directly, so nothing needs to be
activated. R scripts run without `--vanilla` so that `.Rprofile` activates the
renv library.

## Docker

```bash
make docker-build
make docker-test                                  # make check in the image
docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/work {{project_name}} make all   # pipeline on the mounted repo
```

Private inputs are excluded from the image by `.dockerignore`; mount the
repository to use them.

## Changing dependencies

Import the package in code, install it into the environment, then:

```bash
make pin          # environment.yml from imports, renv.lock from R references
```

Commit the regenerated pins together with the code that needs them.
